    "status": "present",
    "value": "Return a shortest valid movement/selection sequence spelling target on the alphabet board, including its single-cell z row. The approach is: move up/left before down/right to avoid invalid cells around z; Manhattan-shortest moves. Its target cost is O(target length) time/output. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
